  <file path="src/main/fetch-comments.ts" change-type="added" viewed="true">
    <comment new-line-start="130" new-line-end="130" severity="major" confidence="high">
      <body>Deleted files are assigned the sentinel path `/dev/null`: `DiffFile.newPath` is `/dev/null` for deletions and is truthy, so `diffFile.newPath || diffFile.oldPath` selects it. For a remote diff deleting `src/old.ts`, `fetch-comments` therefore writes a deleted file entry at `/dev/null`; any fetched comment anchored to `src/old.ts` is then placed in a separate synthetic `modified` entry. This produces incorrect review XML and violates the headless subcommand requirement to serialize the materialized diff and its threads.</body>
      <category>defect</category>
      <suggestion>
        <original-code>    const path = diffFile.newPath || diffFile.oldPath;</original-code>
        <proposed-code>    const path = diffFile.changeType === 'deleted' ? diffFile.oldPath : diffFile.newPath;</proposed-code>
      </suggestion>
    </comment>
  </file>
  <file path="src/main/git-diff-loader.ts" change-type="modified" viewed="true" />
  <file path="src/main/ipc-handlers.test.ts" change-type="modified" viewed="true" />
  <file path="src/main/ipc-handlers.ts" change-type="modified" viewed="true" />
  <file path="src/main/main.ts" change-type="modified" viewed="true" />
  <file path="src/main/remote-mode.test.ts" change-type="added" viewed="true" />
  <file path="src/main/remote-mode.ts" change-type="added" viewed="true">
    <comment new-line-start="215" new-line-end="218" severity="major" confidence="high">
      <body>A temporary clone is not cleaned up when diff loading fails after materialization. `startRemoteSession` returns the cleanup callback, but `bootstrapRemoteDiff` calls `d.loadDiff` without a `try`/`catch` or `finally`; if git diff/repository loading rejects, bootstrap never returns the session. On CLI startup, `main.ts` assigns `remoteCleanup` only after `bootstrapRemoteDiff` succeeds, so the process exit handler also has no callback to invoke. A concrete git-diff failure after a successful temp clone leaves that clone on disk, violating the explicit requirement that temporary clones be removed on every exit path.</body>
      <category>requirement-conformance</category>
    </comment>
  </file>
